t the parks  is something that is reasonably doable  to just kind of copy over the layouts  and then add all of the trees etc by the  way the trees is also one of those  things where I wanted to not download  too much so I'm really just using a  couple of trees throughout the city so  remember it's not really gonna look all  that good on a ground level I just  decided to go for these trees because  they're quite detailed and I think they  have the right kind of color which works  out for the sort of boreal environment  of the city and I think it's one of the  trees that looks best if you look at the  city from an aerial perspective so  that's kind of the reasoning behind that  oh and yeah this area is also kind of  complicated for now I should note that  actually there is slightly different  thing with this under  run tunnel highway then the real-life  situation is in real life the highway  kind of stays underground there's just  an area where the roof is kind of open  so even though you can see the Cedar  Road from this guy it's still like  sunken into the ground and in my in this  case I made it so that actually comes up  to the ground and has an intersection  with the road I might change that but  the problem is that in real life the  highway stays on the ground but it's got  like these retaining walls on the sides  and there's already buildings right next  to it so it's a really dense area in a  way that's impossible to recreate in  city skylines at least not without  having all kinds of mods and assets to  fix that up so that's an area which  isn't entirely as realistic as I'd hoped  it'd be in any case that's it for this  episode I hope I wasn't complaining  about everything too much I just I just  want to kind of keep the expectations  down a little bit these videos are  really just something that I want to  share to kind of get the creative  process of how this is all made in video  form and kind of share how I do this  kind of thing but at the same time it's  really not quite similar to other cities  skylines projects on youtube right now  in a sense that it's not so much about  the way that the city looks but really  just that it functions as a real life  Oslo and then it's a believable copy so  I just want to kind of manage the  expectations in that way that said next  episode is gonna be my favorite episode  it's the episode in which I finally gets  to the area of a cannon or the future of  Indian area which is a part of the city  with lots of highway tunnels and  roundabouts and car retailers I know  that sounds kind of weird but from an  aerial perspective and from a game  perspective it's a super interesting  area and it's been the biggest challenge  by far in recreating Oslo since it's  really complicated when it comes to the  road works so I'm definitely gonna be  happy to share that area in the next  episode but I'm afraid you're gonna have  to wait for the next episode to see that  so thanks for watching guys and I hope  to see you next time  [Music]
 

